the replication-exclusion clause and the wire-compatibility-signal clause have no implementation and no clause of Section 3.3 is enumerated.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n      \\\"keys\\\": [\\n        \\\"section:7.4\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"production\\\": {\\n        \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/catalog/catalog.go\\\",\\n        \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"ForRelease\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n        \\\"catalog-v050-exact\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"unevidenced\\\",\\n      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"ForRelease only returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 7.4; no clause of 7.4 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 1 obligations it carries.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n      \\\"keys\\\": [\\n        \\\"section:7.5\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"production\\\": {\\n        \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/catalog/catalog.go\\\",\\n        \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"ForRelease\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n        \\\"catalog-v050-exact\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"unevidenced\\\",\\n      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"ForRelease only returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 7.5; no clause of 7.5 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 53 obligations it carries.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n      \\\"keys\\\": [\\n        \\\"section:7.A\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"production\\\": {\\n        \\\"path\\\": \\\"internal/catalog/catalog.go\\\",\\n        \\\"declaration\\\": \\\"ForRelease\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"acceptance_cases\\\": [\\n        \\\"catalog-v050-exact\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"unevidenced\\\",\\n      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"ForRelease only returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 7.A; no clause of 7.A is enumerate