{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c51b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07060-dc53-7421-8823-10572f5f580f"},"sequence":232,"recorded_at":1780531400000459,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"1bd0f4b7-3d42-45e7-aae9-47d49f725647","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"1bd0f4b7-3d42-45e7-aae9-47d49f725647","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"1bd0f4b7-3d42-45e7-aae9-47d49f725647"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"8237d78f-de05-46ef-b969-091d44f22519"},"task_id":"8237d78f-de05-46ef-b969-091d44f22519","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"8237d78f-de05-46ef-b969-091d44f22519","chunk":"Read text file `internal/provhost/refusal_arm_inventory_test.go`.\n1|package provhost\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"context\"\n5|\t\"encoding/json\"\n6|\t\"errors\"\n7|\t\"fmt\"\n8|\t\"go/ast\"\n9|\t\"go/parser\"\n10|\t\"go/token\"\n11|\t\"os\"\n12|\t\"path/filepath\"\n13|\t\"sort\"\n14|\t\"strconv\"\n15|\t\"strings\"\n16|\t\"testing\"\n17|\t\"time\"\n18|\n19|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n20|)\n21|\n22|// This file is the derived refusal-arm inventory. It exists because the\n23|// constructor call-site audit in inventory_test.go enumerates constructor\n24|// call SITES, and every frameFault literal and every integrity(...) detail\n25|// funnels through a shared site: planting a new arm through an existing\n26|// site (a new &frameFault literal in checkResponseMembers, a new\n27|// integrity(...) detail in DecodeStatusOutcome) leaves the whole suite\n28|// green. Two review rounds each missed a row by hand, so the arm set is\n29|// derived from production source by parsing it, never by listing it.\n30|//\n31|// Derivation (deriveRefusalArms): every &frameFault{...} literal yields\n32|// frame|<detail>|<member source>; every integrity(...) call with a string\n33|// literal yields integrity|<detail>; the single wrapping site\n34|// integrity(\"status body is \"+fault.detail, ...) expands over the derived\n35|// frame detail set, so each wrapped refusal is its own obligation; every\n36|// rejection branch of parseMajor (a return 0, false) yields\n37|// parse|<enclosing condition source>; every literal first argument to one\n38|// of the six refusal constructors yields ctor|<constructor>|<detail>.\n39|// A non-literal frameFault detail or integrity argument lands as an\n40|// expr:<source> obligation rather than passing silently; a non-literal\n41|// constructor first argument is a fault conduit (fault.detail, a detail\n42|// variable) whose arms are the frame arms above, so it carries no\n43|// separate obligation by design. A missing parseMajor fails the\n44|// derivation outright.\n45|//\n46|// Both directions are checked: TestDerivedRefusalArmsAreAllWitnessed\n47|// (every derived arm carries a witness) and\n48|// TestWitnessedArmsAreAllDerived (every witness names a derived arm, so a\n49|// truncated derivation reddens on the orphaned witnesses instead of\n50|// passing vacuously). TestEveryArmWitnessRefusesAtTheProductionEntry\n51|// drives each witness through the production entry and requires the\n52|// refusal to come from the arm under test. Empty, single-file, or\n53|// unparseable derivations fail closed: a domain that silently derives\n54|// nothing is not a measurement.\n55|//\n56|// Stated bound: arms sharing one (constructor, detail) identity merge to\n57|// one obligation (the two timeout sites, the two empty-response sites,\n58|// the six identical \"not a JSON object\" sites). Deleting one of a merged\n59|// pair is a behavioral mutant the entry-point tests must catch, not this\n60|// inventory.\n61|\n62|// refusalArmCensusFloor is the derived arm count this test was written\n63|// against. It is a tripwire, not an enumeration: a derivation returning\n64|// fewer arms fails closed even when every surviving arm is witnessed,\n65|// which is what catches a silently truncated scan. Raising it is routine\n66|// when production gains a refusal; lowering it requires saying why.\n67|//\n68|// Raised 60 -> 162 by the operation-layer leaf (manifest, probe,\n69|// profile, quiescence, spawn, identity, idempotency decoders), each\n70|// new arm witnessed in declaredOperationWitnesses below.\n71|const refusalArmCensusFloor = 162\n72|\n73|func deriveRefusalArms(t *testing.T) map[string]struct{} {\n74|\tt.Helper()\n75|\tdirectory, err := os.Getwd()\n76|\tif err != nil {\n77|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"derive refusal arms: %v\", err)\n78|\t}\n79|\tarms, scanned, err := refusalArmsIn(directory)\n80|\tif err != nil {\n81|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"derive refusal arms: %v\", err)\n82|\t}\n83|\tif len(scanned) == 0 {\n84|\t\tt.Fatal(\"derived refusal arms from zero production files; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n85|\t}\n86|\tif len(arms) == 0 {\n87|\t\tt.Fatal(\"derived zero refusal arms from the package sources; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n88|\t}\n89|\tif len(arms) < refusalArmCensusFloor {\n90|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"derived %d refusal arms, below the %d census floor; the derivation is short, not the package\", len(arms), refusalArmCensusFloor)\n91|\t}\n92|\tt.Logf(\"refusal arm coverage domain: %d derived arms across %d production files\", len(arms), len(scanned))\n93|\treturn arms\n94|}\n95|\n96|func refusalArmsIn(directory string) (map[string]struct{}, []string, error) {\n97|\tentries, err := os.ReadDir(directory)\n98|\tif err != nil {\n99|\t\treturn nil, nil, err\n100|\t}\n101|\tarms := map[string]struct{}{}\n102|\tvar scanned []string\n103|\tparseBranches := 0\n104|\tfileSet := token.NewFileSet()\n105|\ttype productionFile struct {\n106|\t\tsyntax *ast.File\n107|\t\tsource []byte\n108|\t}\n109|\tvar files []productionFile\n110|\tfor _, entry := range entries {\n111|\t\tname := entry.Name()\n112|\t\tif entry.IsDir() || !strings.HasSuffix(name, \".go\") || strings.HasSuffix(name, \"_test.go\") {\n113|\t\t\tcontinue\n114|\t\t}\n115|\t\tscanned = append(scanned, name)\n116|\t\tpath := filepath.Join(directory, name)\n117|\t\tsource, err := os.ReadFile(path)\n118|\t\tif err != nil {\n119|\t\t\treturn nil, nil, err\n120|\t\t}\n(more lines below)"}}}
