{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d355","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07060-dc53-7421-8823-10572f5f580f"},"sequence":2053,"recorded_at":1780531400004101,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"1bd0f4b7-3d42-45e7-aae9-47d49f725647","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"1bd0f4b7-3d42-45e7-aae9-47d49f725647","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"1bd0f4b7-3d42-45e7-aae9-47d49f725647"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"daf49e0c-0167-41df-97d4-8e00e38949bf"},"task_id":"daf49e0c-0167-41df-97d4-8e00e38949bf","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"daf49e0c-0167-41df-97d4-8e00e38949bf","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-73-1\",\n  \"command\": \"cat >> LOGBOOK.md <<'EOF'\\n\\n### 2321 — A local copy of a shared gate needs a pin, not a comment; a registry that only counts itself cannot see new code\\n- ROOT CAUSE (B3): `provhost.decodeStrictObject` re-implemented strict decoding without the shared `canonicaljson` surrogate rule, and Go's `encoding/json` replaces a lone `\\\\ud800` escape with U+FFFD silently — so Section 1.6 wire bodies carrying lone surrogates were admitted. Same class as the sibling story's decoder gap.\\n- FIX: local `hasLoneSurrogateEscape` gate in `internal/provhost/surrogate.go` (local copy because `canonicaljson` is frozen across both unlanded stories), called first from `decodeStrictObject`; one `\\\\ud800` fixture per production entry plus `TestSurrogateGateAgreesWithCanonicalJSON`, a 13-vector pin driving both the local gate and `canonicaljson.Canonicalize` so the copies cannot drift.\\n- ANOMALY: the first gate version used `switch` and reddened `TestAllProductionSwitchesAreClassified` — the package census bans switches as membership-gate hiding spots. Rewritten with if/else, identical verdicts, green. A gate's own residue rules apply to the fix too.\\n- ROOT CAUSE (B4): `tracecheck` verifies registry -> code only, so ~3,700 lines of `internal/provider` + `internal/provhost` landed with the gate green under gap prose asserting \\\"no provider manifest is implemented anywhere\\\". The census enumerates what registered itself.\\n- FIX: 4 acceptance cases + 4 section bindings (7.1, 7.6, 7.7, 8), 4 gap rewrites (5.5, 7.2, 7.3, 7.5), re-pinned hash; report now bindings=53 unevidenced=45 clauses 17/428. Reverse scan (every `internal/*` package owned or explicitly excluded) recorded as open work, not implemented here.\\n- DECISION (A2/A3/A4, recorded in code): CheckIdentity duplication is deliberate (different error surface, shared package frozen); Provider Protocol 3.0.0 is a stated non-owner bound, not a defect; provider's cause-appending errors must be rebuilt, not quoted, at the future cmd/ax lift (`refuseCausalLeak`).\\n- SCOPE: `internal/provhost/surrogate*.go`, `protocol.go`, refusal inventory (floor 162->164), `profile_test.go` (cross-plane set test), `identity.go`/`doc.go` bounds, `internal/provider/doc.go` composition contract, ownership registry + pin + report/golden/README figures.\\n- STATUS: Resolved. `go test ./...` and `-cover` green, vet + GOOS=windows vet + gofmt clean, admit-all and narrowing mutants red as required. TASK-260830-32jeti round-4, handed to review.\\nEOF\\necho appended\",\n  \"description\": \"Append logbook entry 2321\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"appended\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 9,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 3,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
